meta {
  name: List what an external service affects
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/monitoring-checks/:monitoringCheck_id/affected
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  monitoringCheck_id: 
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  For a monitor that watches a third-party status page: the DNS zones, domains, monitors, servers and status page components of yours that depend on that service. Each has a `source` of `manual` (linked by you) or `auto` (detected by InfraNest at the matching provider: its DNS zones, domains and servers, and your own monitors behind it). An `auto` monitor carries `via`, how it sits behind the provider: `proxy` (its host is a record proxied through it), `dns` (its host is in a DNS zone there), `server` (it watches a server there) or `linked` (you linked it, its server, its zone, its domain or a status page component it feeds to this status monitor). A status page component is named with its page. Servers are listed only when you may read servers.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
